# License scope

Copyright © 2026 The Krabka Authors. Existing source-specific notices remain in force.

This repository contains material under different licenses. A license applies
by material type, not by file extension. The licenses below are not a choice
of either license for every file. Existing third-party notices and explicit
source-specific terms take precedence over these defaults.

## Original website code and code samples

Original website code is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(SPDX: Apache-2.0). This includes templates, CSS, scripts, build configuration,
and browser-tool code.

Original code samples in documentation and other pages are also Apache-2.0.
A sample remains Apache-2.0 when it appears in a file whose surrounding prose
is CC BY 4.0. The surrounding explanation does not change the sample's license.

Read the complete terms in [LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt](LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt).

## Original prose

Original documentation and other website prose are licensed under Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International (SPDX: CC-BY-4.0).

Read the complete terms in [LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt](LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt).
Read [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md#licenses-and-attribution) for attribution
instructions and the terms for incoming contributions.

## Brand artwork and trademarks

Original Krabka brand artwork, including the logo, wordmark, lockups, favicons,
and their generated previews, retains its existing Apache-2.0 copyright
license. This makes the artwork boundary explicit; it is not CC BY prose.
The existing brand page states the Apache-2.0 treatment of the marks.

Copyright permission does not grant trademark rights. Read
[trademark.md](trademark.md) before using the Krabka name or marks. No statement
here identifies a new copyright owner or claims trademark registration.

## Third-party and imported material

Imported material keeps its source license and attribution. This scope map
does not relicense dependencies, bundled assets, synced documentation, generated
reference material, proof inputs, charts, or third-party code samples.

The checked-in notices include:

- Inter and JetBrains Mono fonts: SIL Open Font License 1.1 in
  [public/fonts/LICENSE-inter.txt](public/fonts/LICENSE-inter.txt) and
  [public/fonts/LICENSE-jetbrains-mono.txt](public/fonts/LICENSE-jetbrains-mono.txt).
- Devicon language icons: MIT terms in
  [public/icons/languages/LICENSE](public/icons/languages/LICENSE).
- Imported kafkactl code: BSD 3-Clause terms in
  [kafkactl-lab/LICENSE.fgrosse-kafkactl](kafkactl-lab/LICENSE.fgrosse-kafkactl).
- Vendored compression crate: its own
  [LICENSE](playground/vendor/krabka-compression/LICENSE) and
  [NOTICE](playground/vendor/krabka-compression/NOTICE), including upstream notices.

Documentation synced into src/content/docs/ and proof material synced from
component repositories retain the source repository's terms. Published charts
in public/charts/ retain their source terms. The Why3/prover build scripts copy
upstream licenses into each generated bundle's LICENSES/ directory; keep those
licenses with the bundle. Installed npm, Rust, Go, and other dependencies keep
their own licenses, including when bundled into distributed output.

This is a scope inventory, not a complete dependency-license audit. Do not infer
a new license grant for material with unclear provenance. Preserve source
notices and resolve unclear terms before adding or redistributing that material.
